# Analytics

A new [Analytics](/analytics) section is now available. It gives an overview of how things are evolving, from one year to the next, using the data already in CSA Admin.

Open it from the chart icon in the top right, between the support and handbook icons. The same links are also in the footer.

[Memberships](/analytics/memberships) and [billing](/analytics/billing) are always there: how many memberships and how many renew, the mix of sizes, depots, and cycles, invoiced amounts, payments, and time to pay.

Other pages appear when you use those features:

- [Absences](/analytics/absences): declarations, absence rate, and included quota
- [Member participation](/analytics/activities): demanded and accepted participations
- [<%= BasketContent.model_name.human %>](/analytics/basket_content): coverage and products
- [Shop](/analytics/shop): orders and amounts

Obviously, the longer you have used CSA Admin, the more interesting this data becomes 😉.

This is a first iteration. Don't hesitate to [contact me](/support) if something looks off, or if you have an idea for a chart to add.
